  Metabolic flux distributions were estimated using the RIPTiDe algorithm (https://github.com/mjenior/riptide), with 1,000 flux samples generated for each model. Input models derived from ftINIT were used for flux estimation.  
  The resulting flux distributions were further analyzed to quantify differences between conditions using Cliff’s delta and to identify key reactions using a random forest model.  
  Scripts for flux sampling, statistical analysis, and visualization, along with the corresponding results, are provided in this directory.
